value.string:
{
 "type": "function",
 "function": {
 "name": "ERP5Document_doAction",
 "description": "Perform any action on a module or document: create a new document inside it, invoke a workflow transition (e.g. 'plan', 'confirm', 'start', 'stop', 'validate', 'deliver'), invoke a custom object action, or save edits to a document's own fields (action_id 'edit'). Call ERP5Document_getActionList on the same relative_url first to find which action_id values are currently valid (including 'add <portal_type>' entries built from can_create_here, and 'edit' from object_view_list). If that action opens a dialog, its fields (dialog_field_list) are automatically pre-filled with their own default/current values before invoking - you only need to pass keyword arguments for the fields whose value you want to override (for 'add <portal_type>' or 'edit', they become the document's field values, using the plain property id with any 'my_' prefix removed; a relation field, whose id usually ends in '_value', takes the related document's relative_url as a string). IMPORTANT: before calling this with dry_run=false, look at the dialog_field_list you got from ERP5Document_getActionList for this exact action_id and decide, for each field, whether the user already gave you a value for it (a title, a description, an amount, a related document, etc.) - if so, you MUST pass that field's id (with any 'my_' prefix removed) as a keyword argument here; do not leave it to fall back to its own default/current value, which is very often blank and not what the user asked for. Prefer setting every such field directly in the same 'add <portal_type>' call rather than creating a blank document and editing it afterward. If you call this with no keyword arguments at all, the response includes a warning reminding you to check dialog_field_list again. Every response also includes property_dict, re-read directly from the document after the call (not just an echo of what you sent) - check it to confirm your values actually stuck instead of guessing or repeating the same call.",
 "parameters": {
 "type": "object",
 "properties": {
 "relative_url": {
 "type": "string",
 "description": "relative_url of the module or existing document to act on"
 },
 "action_id": {
 "type": "string",
 "description": "id of the action to invoke: a workflow transition (e.g. 'confirm', 'start', 'validate'), a custom object action, 'add <portal_type>' (e.g. 'add Purchase Order Line') to create a new document of that portal_type inside relative_url, or 'edit' to save edits to relative_url's own fields"
 },
 "dry_run": {
 "type": "boolean",
 "description": "If true (default), do not invoke or create anything: just return a preview. Set to false to actually do it."
 }
 },
 "required": [
 "relative_url",
 "action_id"
 ]
 }
 }
 }
